C1   liveness: guest ran, plain RAM readback  got=-            want=0x11223344   FAIL
C2   MMU really OFF in arm L (CP15 c1 bit 0)  got=-            want=0x00000000   FAIL
C3   MMU really ON in arm T (the arms differ) got=-            want=0x00000001   FAIL
C4   MMU-on arm CANNOT see the device         got=-            want=!= 0x1011    FAIL
      *** THE DISCRIMINATOR IS DEAD: the device answered with the boot-time MMU
      *** still enabled, so arm L proves nothing about turning it off.  Either the
      *** cats translation table changed (machine_cats.c:131, cpu_arm.c:239-255)
      *** or the device moved into the low 256 MB.  Re-derive before believing A1/A2.
C5   MMU-on arm SURVIVES, exit 0              status=NO-PROMPT exit=1        FAIL
A1   VENDOR_ID through a real guest ldr       got=-            want=0x00001011   FAIL
A2   TIMER_1_LOAD masked to 24 bits (MAX_VAL) got=-            want=0x00345678   FAIL
      *** THE MMU TRAP, and A1/A2 are NOT evidence about the device: arm L's
      *** CP15 c1 bit 0 is still SET, so VA 0x42000000 aliased to PA 0x02000000
      *** (machine_cats.c:131 -> cpu_arm.c:239-255 maps only the low 256 MB) and
      *** nothing ever addressed the footbridge.  Fix the MMU-off sequence first.
